\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a) One checkpoint under two conditioning contexts. At the root it prefers to refuse; once an unsafe prefix has accumulated---through a prefill, a jailbreak, tool or retrieved content, or multi-turn drift---it prefers the harmful continuation from the reached state \(s_t=x\oplus h_{\leq t}\). Stroke weight marks the preferred branch in each band, and the dashed arrow marks the reversal. CURE-DPO{} scores the lower band only, holding \(s_t\) byte-for-byte fixed and optimizing the ordering of its alternative futures. (b) Fraction of \((\text  {prompt},\text  {state})\) pairs with a positive root margin but a negative same-state margin, with seed standard deviations over three runs.}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:reversal}{{1}{2}{(a) One checkpoint under two conditioning contexts. At the root it prefers to refuse; once an unsafe prefix has accumulated---through a prefill, a jailbreak, tool or retrieved content, or multi-turn drift---it prefers the harmful continuation from the reached state \(s_t=x\oplus h_{\leq t}\). Stroke weight marks the preferred branch in each band, and the dashed arrow marks the reversal. \method {} scores the lower band only, holding \(s_t\) byte-for-byte fixed and optimizing the ordering of its alternative futures. (b) Fraction of \((\text {prompt},\text {state})\) pairs with a positive root margin but a negative same-state margin, with seed standard deviations over three runs}{figure.caption.1}{}}
