\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces CURE-DPO{} changes which states are compared and what they are compared against---the outlined zone, stages 1--2; how the resulting pairs are optimized (stages 3--4) is standard. \textbf  {1}~Six candidate states per prompt: five fixed depths and one hard state mined where the frozen base model most prefers the harmful branch. \textbf  {2}~Both branches decode from one byte-for-byte identical reached state \(s_t\), and four filters accept \(67.7\%\) of the proposed pairs. \textbf  {3}~Only the branch tokens are scored, so the shared prefix cancels and the loss is unchanged from DPO (Appendix~\ref {app:algorithm}). \textbf  {4}~Gradients follow a prompt's two highest-loss states, selected from detached values, together with clean-safety and benign anchors. The frozen base checkpoint, later reused as \(\pi _{\mathrm  {ref}}\), writes every recovery branch.}}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{2}{4}{\method {} changes which states are compared and what they are compared against---the outlined zone, stages 1--2; how the resulting pairs are optimized (stages 3--4) is standard. \textbf {1}~Six candidate states per prompt: five fixed depths and one hard state mined where the frozen base model most prefers the harmful branch. \textbf {2}~Both branches decode from one byte-for-byte identical reached state \(s_t\), and four filters accept \(67.7\%\) of the proposed pairs. \textbf {3}~Only the branch tokens are scored, so the shared prefix cancels and the loss is unchanged from DPO (Appendix~\ref {app:algorithm}). \textbf {4}~Gradients follow a prompt's two highest-loss states, selected from detached values, together with clean-safety and benign anchors. The frozen base checkpoint, later reused as \(\pi _{\mathrm {ref}}\), writes every recovery branch}{figure.caption.6}{}}
