\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Design space of recovery-oriented defenses. US: conditions on the unsafe state. RK: ranks a chosen continuation against a rejected continuation. SS: both are conditioned on a byte-for-byte identical unsafe prefix. HM: hard-state mining. TW: tail weighting. \(\ast \) the harmful branch enters through an unlearning rather than a ranking term; -- not applicable. Entries characterize each method as published, and a method may reach a related effect by other means. Backtracking's DPO variant ranks a \texttt  {[RESET]}-and-restart continuation against the harmful continuation from the same unsafe prefix, so it already satisfies US, RK, and SS; it differs from CURE-DPO{} in restarting rather than recovering in place, and in neither selecting nor weighting states. Rows are \citet  {dai2023saferlhf}, \citet  {qi2024safety}, \citet  {zhao2025door}, \citet  {zhang2024backtracking}, \citet  {zou2024circuit}, and \citet  {park2026trajectory}.}}{19}{table.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:related}{{10}{19}{Design space of recovery-oriented defenses. US: conditions on the unsafe state. RK: ranks a chosen continuation against a rejected continuation. SS: both are conditioned on a byte-for-byte identical unsafe prefix. HM: hard-state mining. TW: tail weighting. \(\ast \) the harmful branch enters through an unlearning rather than a ranking term; -- not applicable. Entries characterize each method as published, and a method may reach a related effect by other means. Backtracking's DPO variant ranks a \texttt {[RESET]}-and-restart continuation against the harmful continuation from the same unsafe prefix, so it already satisfies US, RK, and SS; it differs from \method {} in restarting rather than recovering in place, and in neither selecting nor weighting states. Rows are \citet {dai2023saferlhf}, \citet {qi2024safety}, \citet {zhao2025door}, \citet {zhang2024backtracking}, \citet {zou2024circuit}, and \citet {park2026trajectory}}{table.caption.48}{}}
